From fcefdcf0f33ad4a5414e0f665907cb9424ececfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <ms178@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:06:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] aarch64: full-precision carrier plumbing (f128_softfloat
 SIGSEGV + wrong -a)

Three interlocking defects, all rooted in the same blind spot: values
lowered to the IrType::U128 _Float128 carrier carry 16 REAL bytes, but
several backend paths treated untracked U128 data as an f64 to be
extended, or truncated it to its low qword.

1. eliminate_unused_x9_address_moves deleted `mov x9, xN` on a
   single-instruction lookahead. After eliminate_move_chains folds the
   chain (mov x9,x20 -> mov x9,x0) and propagate_register_copies
   rewrites only the FIRST use (ldr x0,[x9] -> ldr x0,[x0]), the next
   line looks clean while the second load of a 16-byte global carrier
   (ldr x1,[x9,#8]) still reads x9 -> stale-register SIGSEGV. The pass
   now scans to the first x9 read (mov kept), pure x9 redefinition
   (mov dead), control-flow boundary, call (x9 caller-saved), or
   function end before believing the mov is dead.

2. F128Neg/F128Fabs/F128Copysign operand staging degraded untracked
   carrier arguments to the __extenddftf2(low qword) fallback: -1.5F128
   materialized as -0.0. U128 loads now record their destination as a
   full-precision f128 source (track_f128_self), so the existing
   tracked-source path stages all 16 bytes.

3. operand_to_x0_x1 loaded tracked F128 values by value type (8 bytes,
   high half zeroed) when a U128-typed consumer asked for the pair,
   truncating carrier results stored through U128-typed Stores. The
   pair load now prefers the f128 tracker (direct and indirect homes),
   and IrConst::LongDouble constants stage bit-exactly instead of
   integer-reinterpreting the binary128 pattern. U128 stores of tracked
   values propagate the tracking to the destination slot.

Validation: f128_softfloat rc=0 (was 139); new f128_global_carrier
regression (GOT-load + negation + double negation, GCC-oracle parity);
three new mutation-verified peephole unit tests (the survivor test
fails against the old lookahead, verified by temporary revert);
lib 1273/0/6; ARM 373 passed / 33 failed / 75 skipped (was 371/34,
no regressions); x86 536/5 unchanged (5 pre-existing).
