From 9243b80f8dd401f84ea49db7e497457098e1cd87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <ms178@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:25:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] arm, riscv: scalar FP round/fma/copysign intrinsics (were
 silently dropped)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

RoundScalarF64/F32, FmaScalarF64/F32 and CopysignF64/F32 were lowered
only on x86 (ROUNDSD/VFMA/VANDPD); aarch64 and riscv64 fell into the
intrinsics catch-all and emitted NOTHING, so rint/floor/ceil/trunc/
copysign/fma read uninitialized registers and returned 0.0 (observed:
vex_move_false_dep outputs DIFFER on both, any math.h-heavy code broken).

  * aarch64: native FRINTN/M/P/Z (x86 ROUND imm8 modes map 1:1: 0=nearest-
    even, 1=floor(-inf), 2=ceil(+inf), 3=trunc(zero)), FMADD, and sign-bit
    and/or on the F64/F32 patterns for copysign.
  * riscv64: FMADD.d/S and FSGNJ.d/S are native; the mode-selecting round
    has no RV64D instruction, so route through the libm symbols (rint/
    floor/ceil/trunc[f]) exactly as GCC's unfolded builtins do — fa0 is
    the F64 ABI argument register.
  * each staged operand bridges through t0 on riscv (operand_to_t0's only
    target); the initial version bridged ft1/ft2 from stale t1/t2.

New self-checking differential test scalar_fp_builtins (no libm needed
on aarch64; -lm on riscv64 for the rounding symbols). Validation:
aarch64 + riscv64 outputs byte-match GCC on vex_move_false_dep and the
new test; ARM suite 375/32/75 (was 373/33); x86 suite 537/5 (test added);
lib 1273/0/6.
